[Music]  british iranian aid worker nazarene  zagari ratcliffe has been sentenced to  another year in jail by an iranian  courts  sakai ratcliffe had been released from  prison in march after serving  five years on charges of plotting  against the government  well her latest jail term comes from a  new charge of spreading  propaganda against iran she and her  family have always denied  the allegations against her well paul  brennan  is live in london joins us from outside  the  iranian embassy paul what's happening  with these  latest charges she's been accused of  plotting against  iran presumably from inside a prison  cell what's going on  well no it's um the reason why we're  here is because it's here  that uh nazim zagari ratcliff's  alleged offense is supposed to have  taken place uh  2009 uh in in anti-government  protests here outside the iranian  embassy naznagari radcliffe  participated in protests and gave an  interview to bbc  persian and now 12 years on uh the  iranians have decided to prosecute her  for this despite the fact that she's  already gone through the  uh system for the other charges um which  she denied  she denies these charges as well but on  march the 14th  in a 20-minute hearing behind closed  doors they  tried her for this offense and have now  decided that she will be sentenced to  another year  in prison i have to say that she's not  been ordered back to jail  yet so technically she's not behind bars  um the other aspect of it is that she's  not allowed to leave  iran uh for another year um her lawyer  has said that they will be appealing  against this verdict a time scale for  that legal process  hasn't been yet laid out but from here  at the iranian embassy i knocked on the  door just before we came on  air and i've submitted an email with a  request for a statement from them but no  statement has yet been forthcoming from  the embassy here  so what's this really uh about then paul  because uh  sagari ratcliffe's husband is very high  profile in his campaign to to get his  wife released and to  to to bring her back home essentially  has there been any reaction from him  does he think this is about a protest  that took place  on british soil or is there something  else to this  yeah now there's been plenty of reaction  and there's a lot of  uh conjecture and suspicion as to  exactly what is behind  all of this uh let's go to the reaction  first of all of richard  uh ratcliffe uh and he has said uh that  he believes that she's being used as a  negotiating  tactic by the iranian authorities and  he clarified that she hadn't yet been  summoned back to  actual prison the british prime minister  boris johnson has said i don't think  that it's right at all that  she should be sentenced to more time in  jail it's wrong that she was there in  the first place  and he said they're working very hard to  secure her release working with our  american friends  as he described them as well and dominic  robb who is the british foreign  secretary said it was totally  inhumane and totally unjustified this  decision by  the iranian court we continue to call on  iran to release nazim  immediately now as far as the why she is  there  well there are several different stories  um first of all that it's related to  an arms deal death of around 400 million  pounds an order for chieftain tanks that  was made  by the previous shah of iran and those  tanks were never delivered by britain  iran wanting at least their money back  britain  the british government has explicitly  admitted that there is a debt  that really does need to be paid the  question is how to pay it  there are sanctions for example that  prevent money being sent  in in such overt way to iran and the  british and iranians haven't yet found a  way  to have that debt resolved without  falling foul of those sanctions  the other aspect is of course just the  general state  of tension and diplomatic issues that  there are between  uh the west and iran um as regards  sanctions as regard the nuclear deal as  regards many many different things  okay paul brennan there live for us  outside the arena embassy in london  thank you paul

